WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.328 --> 00:00:04.596
- Good morning, believe nation.

00:00:04.596 --> 00:00:07.299
My name is Evan Carmichael,
and my one word is believe,

00:00:07.299 --> 00:00:09.284
and I believe that
entrepreneurs will solve

00:00:09.284 --> 00:00:11.294
all of the major problems in the world.

00:00:11.294 --> 00:00:12.907
So to help you on your journey today,

00:00:12.907 --> 00:00:14.993
we're going to talk
about how you can create

00:00:14.993 --> 00:00:17.097
a massive action plan.

00:00:17.097 --> 00:00:19.225
Rule number three is my personal favorite,

00:00:19.225 --> 00:00:21.938
and I'd love to know which
one you guys like the best.

00:00:21.938 --> 00:00:23.958
And as always, as you're
watching, if you hear something

00:00:23.958 --> 00:00:25.393
that really resonates with you,

00:00:25.393 --> 00:00:27.250
please leave it down
in the comments below,

00:00:27.250 --> 00:00:29.432
put quotes around it so
other people can be inspired.

00:00:29.432 --> 00:00:31.181
You might win a prize too.

00:00:31.181 --> 00:00:33.286
And also, when you write it
down, it's much more likely

00:00:33.286 --> 00:00:35.933
to stick, for yourself, as well.

00:00:35.933 --> 00:00:37.233
Enjoy.

00:00:37.233 --> 00:00:40.150
(Upbeat pop music)

00:00:54.733 --> 00:00:59.046
- Some of you, in the past,
you've gotten momentum,

00:00:59.046 --> 00:01:00.603
you've gotten passionate,

00:01:00.603 --> 00:01:02.768
you've even made a decision,

00:01:02.768 --> 00:01:07.005
but a decision is the first step.

00:01:07.005 --> 00:01:08.931
Decision is like a war.

00:01:08.931 --> 00:01:10.642
I got to do this or that, alright,

00:01:10.642 --> 00:01:12.791
I'm going to make myself do this.

00:01:12.791 --> 00:01:17.023
But commitment is when you
now, after you've decided,

00:01:17.023 --> 00:01:19.629
you commit to do this for the long-term.

00:01:19.629 --> 00:01:21.912
Whether it's hard or easy doesn't matter.

00:01:21.912 --> 00:01:23.840
You're doing this.

00:01:23.840 --> 00:01:25.993
It takes it from this moment,

00:01:25.993 --> 00:01:27.606
and it carries it into the future,

00:01:27.606 --> 00:01:29.245
even when things are difficult.

00:01:29.245 --> 00:01:33.274
Then once you decide, the
only way the commitment

00:01:33.274 --> 00:01:35.480
and the energy, and the
momentum, continues,

00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:38.932
is if you take immediate,
massive, what, my friends?

00:01:38.932 --> 00:01:40.015
Massive what?

00:01:41.011 --> 00:01:43.971
Write down in your notes, massive action

00:01:43.971 --> 00:01:46.570
is the cure-all.

00:01:46.570 --> 00:01:49.153
Massive action is the cure-all.

00:01:50.016 --> 00:01:52.541
If you're having a difficult
time with something,

00:01:52.541 --> 00:01:55.013
your relationship isn't
where you want it to be, your

00:01:55.013 --> 00:01:57.154
finances are not where
you want to be, your body

00:01:57.154 --> 00:01:58.944
is not where you want to be, your business

00:01:58.944 --> 00:02:02.239
is not where you want to be,
you need to take massive action.

00:02:02.239 --> 00:02:03.962
And if that doesn't
work, try something else.

00:02:03.962 --> 00:02:05.319
If that doesn't work, try something else.

00:02:05.319 --> 00:02:07.978
Keep going with massive action,

00:02:07.978 --> 00:02:09.980
and you will find the way, because

00:02:09.980 --> 00:02:12.336
it will give you momentum.

00:02:12.336 --> 00:02:15.253
(light bell music)

00:02:16.494 --> 00:02:19.036
When it comes to planning your life,

00:02:19.036 --> 00:02:22.130
I want to get you to learn
to ask three questions now,

00:02:22.130 --> 00:02:23.832
and the first one is not:
what am I going to do?

00:02:23.832 --> 00:02:25.809
And how many understand why now, say I.

00:02:25.809 --> 00:02:26.666
- [Audience] I.

00:02:26.666 --> 00:02:28.820
- The question you want to ask
yourself is: what do I want?

00:02:28.820 --> 00:02:30.648
What's my outcome, what's my result?

00:02:30.648 --> 00:02:33.633
The word R-P-M, the first one

00:02:33.633 --> 00:02:35.183
is to get you focused on the target.

00:02:35.183 --> 00:02:37.640
The target is not the activity,
the activity can change.

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:40.626
It's, what's the result I'm after?

00:02:40.626 --> 00:02:43.245
If you know exactly what
it is you really want,

00:02:43.245 --> 00:02:46.054
what you desire, what you're really after,

00:02:46.054 --> 00:02:47.856
clarity is power.

00:02:47.856 --> 00:02:50.271
The more clear you are in
specifically what you want,

00:02:50.271 --> 00:02:52.770
the faster your brain can get you there.

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:55.062
But if you're genuinely saying
things like: what do I want?

00:02:55.062 --> 00:02:56.874
Well, I want more money.
Fine.

00:02:56.874 --> 00:02:58.727
Here's a dollar, get out of here.

00:02:58.727 --> 00:03:00.038
(audience laughing)

00:03:00.038 --> 00:03:01.374
Did you achieve the outcome?

00:03:01.374 --> 00:03:03.590
Yeah.
When you're that general,

00:03:03.590 --> 00:03:05.404
you think you're not
getting your goal, you are.

00:03:05.404 --> 00:03:07.064
The way you language your
goal, the way you think

00:03:07.064 --> 00:03:09.709
about it, you're receiving it.

00:03:09.709 --> 00:03:12.611
You know, I want to feel a bit better.

00:03:12.611 --> 00:03:13.898
I want to lose some weight.

00:03:13.898 --> 00:03:15.672
Fine, you lost a pound, you're done.

00:03:15.672 --> 00:03:17.485
'Cause your brain's
like a servo mechanism,

00:03:17.485 --> 00:03:19.161
and a bomb, and a missile.

00:03:19.161 --> 00:03:20.592
The old days, you shoot a missile,

00:03:20.592 --> 00:03:22.778
and the target was going, and
if you missed the trajectory,

00:03:22.778 --> 00:03:23.611
you missed it.

00:03:23.611 --> 00:03:25.108
Today, what happens when the missile

00:03:25.108 --> 00:03:26.970
is not on course, what happens?

00:03:26.970 --> 00:03:29.389
It locks on to the heat
signature, what does it do?

00:03:29.389 --> 00:03:30.726
It moves and follows it.

00:03:30.726 --> 00:03:32.792
That's the way your brain
is, if it knows the outcome,

00:03:32.792 --> 00:03:34.265
if it knows the result.

00:03:34.265 --> 00:03:36.824
So RPM starts with, I
got to know the result,

00:03:36.824 --> 00:03:38.889
this is a results planning system.

00:03:38.889 --> 00:03:40.541
The rapid planning method, you can think

00:03:40.541 --> 00:03:41.736
of it as a results planning system.

00:03:41.736 --> 00:03:43.578
I need to know the result I'm after,

00:03:43.578 --> 00:03:46.045
before I ever ask myself what to do.

00:03:46.045 --> 00:03:48.512
That takes more time,

00:03:48.512 --> 00:03:49.772
but it's worth it.

00:03:49.772 --> 00:03:52.721
And when you think in terms
of outcomes and activities,

00:03:52.721 --> 00:03:54.296
pretty soon, some of the
activities, you'll notice,

00:03:54.296 --> 00:03:55.568
you don't even need to
do to get the outcome.

00:03:55.568 --> 00:03:58.215
You'll find a better way to
get the outcome, quicker.

00:03:58.215 --> 00:03:59.412
Now, how do you do that?

00:03:59.412 --> 00:04:00.342
You ask three questions.

00:04:00.342 --> 00:04:03.597
Question one: what is my result?

00:04:03.597 --> 00:04:04.430
What is my outcome?

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:07.441
What is it that I really,
truly want from this?

00:04:07.441 --> 00:04:10.726
If you're going back next week,
and you say this next week,

00:04:10.726 --> 00:04:12.793
what are the most important, what?

00:04:12.793 --> 00:04:16.155
Outcomes, for me to get
this week, in my business.

00:04:16.155 --> 00:04:17.390
And you just write those outcomes out,

00:04:17.390 --> 00:04:20.199
not your action items, the outcomes.

00:04:20.199 --> 00:04:22.354
If you do that and nothing else,

00:04:22.354 --> 00:04:23.791
you'll be ahead of the game.

00:04:23.791 --> 00:04:25.730
And if you just keep looking
at those outcomes every day.

00:04:25.730 --> 00:04:27.106
How am I doing on that outcome?

00:04:27.106 --> 00:04:29.121
Your brain will come up with
ways to get to that outcome,

00:04:29.121 --> 00:04:29.954
I promise you.

00:04:29.954 --> 00:04:33.780
Focus on the outcomes, not on activities.

00:04:33.780 --> 00:04:36.732
Action, for most people, activities,

00:04:36.732 --> 00:04:41.302
most people mistake
movement for achievement.

00:04:41.302 --> 00:04:44.849
They mistake action items
and to-do's for achievement.

00:04:44.849 --> 00:04:46.049
We're after the achievement.

00:04:46.049 --> 00:04:47.341
Are you with me on this?
Yes or no.

00:04:47.341 --> 00:04:48.174
- [Audience] Yes.

00:04:48.174 --> 00:04:49.550
- It's a different way of thinking,

00:04:49.550 --> 00:04:52.286
and I think all of you
inherently have it, but if you

00:04:52.286 --> 00:04:54.765
make this ritualized, just
like the things you've learned

00:04:54.765 --> 00:04:56.417
this week, they're all great,

00:04:56.417 --> 00:04:58.369
but if you don't systematize them,

00:04:58.369 --> 00:04:59.844
they'll work when you do 'em.

00:04:59.844 --> 00:05:01.923
Why is more important than how.

00:05:01.923 --> 00:05:03.016
Why are we doing this?

00:05:03.016 --> 00:05:04.681
What's the purpose?

00:05:04.681 --> 00:05:07.764
Purpose is more powerful than object.

00:05:08.598 --> 00:05:11.533
Purpose is more powerful than object.

00:05:11.533 --> 00:05:12.904
You say I want a million dollars.

00:05:12.904 --> 00:05:14.052
That's a great objective.

00:05:14.052 --> 00:05:15.464
I want a billion dollars, great objective.

00:05:15.464 --> 00:05:19.189
I want to feed 3,000
children in my community,

00:05:19.189 --> 00:05:22.175
that's a beautiful objective,
it's even more specific.

00:05:22.175 --> 00:05:24.631
But even that objective,
you might get excited

00:05:24.631 --> 00:05:28.044
about, 'till you realize what
it takes to feed 3,000 kids.

00:05:28.044 --> 00:05:29.065
Right?

00:05:29.065 --> 00:05:31.092
And the politics involved,
and all the people

00:05:31.092 --> 00:05:32.617
that don't follow through.

00:05:32.617 --> 00:05:33.966
And then you have this good intention,

00:05:33.966 --> 00:05:35.604
and somebody else is pissed off because

00:05:35.604 --> 00:05:37.710
one of the kids didn't get fed.

00:05:37.710 --> 00:05:39.272
(audience laughing)
Right?

00:05:39.272 --> 00:05:41.123
And you didn't even know
what you're going to do.

00:05:41.123 --> 00:05:42.886
What's going to make you keep going?

00:05:42.886 --> 00:05:43.719
Purpose.

00:05:44.589 --> 00:05:46.489
Why do we want to feed those 3,000 kids?

00:05:46.489 --> 00:05:48.101
Why do you want to make
that million dollars,

00:05:48.101 --> 00:05:49.136
that billion dollars?

00:05:49.136 --> 00:05:50.985
Why do you want to take your
business to the next level?

00:05:50.985 --> 00:05:52.912
Why is the most important thing to know,

00:05:52.912 --> 00:05:55.032
'cause that's where all the
emotional juice and fuel

00:05:55.032 --> 00:05:56.533
is, to actually get you to go through

00:05:56.533 --> 00:05:58.659
when the challenges show up.

00:05:58.659 --> 00:06:01.872
Every person you see who's
on fire and is successful,

00:06:01.872 --> 00:06:03.545
knows the why.

00:06:03.545 --> 00:06:05.348
You know what the problem is?

00:06:05.348 --> 00:06:06.520
You might know the why at the beginning,

00:06:06.520 --> 00:06:07.906
you wrote a mission statement
and stuff like that.

00:06:07.906 --> 00:06:10.651
You got to know why you're
doing this, right now.

00:06:10.651 --> 00:06:12.414
This, right now.

00:06:12.414 --> 00:06:14.508
That's what's going to engage
you and activate the why.

00:06:14.508 --> 00:06:16.823
You might have a why, but it's not active.

00:06:16.823 --> 00:06:21.461
80% of success is why, 20% is how.

00:06:21.461 --> 00:06:24.513
Get a big enough why, people
will figure out how to do it.

00:06:24.513 --> 00:06:26.818
And once you know the why,
you know what you're after

00:06:26.818 --> 00:06:30.651
and why, then the question
is: how do we do it?

00:06:30.651 --> 00:06:33.429
We know what we're after
and why; how do we do it?

00:06:33.429 --> 00:06:35.884
By the way, are there lots of
how's to get to an outcome?

00:06:35.884 --> 00:06:36.791
Yes or no.

00:06:36.791 --> 00:06:37.986
- Yes.
- Are there many paths

00:06:37.986 --> 00:06:39.600
to get a result, yes or no?
- Yes.

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:41.326
- Some are more efficient than others,

00:06:41.326 --> 00:06:42.599
and you're not going to know, so you know

00:06:42.599 --> 00:06:43.552
what you do, you brainstorm

00:06:43.552 --> 00:06:45.848
out all the how's you can think of.

00:06:45.848 --> 00:06:47.147
All of things you could possibly need

00:06:47.147 --> 00:06:48.192
to do to get that result,

00:06:48.192 --> 00:06:49.793
and then you narrow it down to the 20%

00:06:49.793 --> 00:06:52.161
that makes 80% of the difference, and

00:06:52.161 --> 00:06:54.542
you'll find out you don't have
to do that whole to-do list.

00:06:54.542 --> 00:06:57.112
If fact, wouldn't it be nice
to write your own to-do list

00:06:57.112 --> 00:06:59.417
and not do it, and still get the outcome?

00:06:59.417 --> 00:07:00.689
(audience laughing)

00:07:00.689 --> 00:07:02.266
How many would prefer that?
Say I.

00:07:02.266 --> 00:07:03.245
- [Audience] I.

00:07:03.245 --> 00:07:04.328
- That's RPM.

00:07:05.564 --> 00:07:09.825
I love it when I don't do my
to-dos, and I get the outcome.

00:07:09.825 --> 00:07:11.573
That's the coolest thing in the world.

00:07:11.573 --> 00:07:12.985
You might have done one or two of them,

00:07:12.985 --> 00:07:14.394
but it's then learning selectively

00:07:14.394 --> 00:07:15.894
which ones are going to
create it, but the only one

00:07:15.894 --> 00:07:18.539
you got to brainstorm out, the
M, the massive action plan.

00:07:18.539 --> 00:07:20.543
So if you know the result,
and you know the purpose,

00:07:20.543 --> 00:07:23.476
now you need the M, which
is the massive action plan.

00:07:23.476 --> 00:07:26.400
We also call the massive
action plan, the MAP.

00:07:26.400 --> 00:07:27.774
It's your massive action plan, your map.

00:07:27.774 --> 00:07:29.170
How are you going to get there?

00:07:29.170 --> 00:07:31.043
What are you going to do?

00:07:31.043 --> 00:07:33.265
And by the way, when you're
crystal-clear in what you want,

00:07:33.265 --> 00:07:35.898
and you know why you want
it, you can make a big map.

00:07:35.898 --> 00:07:37.398
You can brainstorm a
million ways to do it.

00:07:37.398 --> 00:07:38.910
Not all your how's are going to work,

00:07:38.910 --> 00:07:40.270
that's why you make a whole map.

00:07:40.270 --> 00:07:42.388
And then go back and
gradually asterisk the ones

00:07:42.388 --> 00:07:45.498
that are the most
important, and go hit those.

00:07:45.498 --> 00:07:47.121
You might get the whole
outcome in the first two

00:07:47.121 --> 00:07:50.569
action items, and get rid of
the whole rest of your list.

00:07:50.569 --> 00:07:51.997
This is RPM.

00:07:51.997 --> 00:07:53.259
This is how I operate.

00:07:53.259 --> 00:07:55.134
Now, if you never did this on paper,

00:07:55.134 --> 00:07:57.211
and you just did this
thinking process in your head,

00:07:57.211 --> 00:07:58.822
you'll get invaluable resources.

00:07:58.822 --> 00:08:00.134
If you learned to put this on paper,

00:08:00.134 --> 00:08:01.721
it'll be more powerful
because then your brain

00:08:01.721 --> 00:08:03.902
isn't racing, and you can see it.

00:08:03.902 --> 00:08:05.941
If you make it into a system
that you personally use,

00:08:05.941 --> 00:08:07.945
your productivity will explode.

00:08:07.945 --> 00:08:10.503
If you teach your whole
company to do this,

00:08:10.503 --> 00:08:12.764
your company will go up
levels you can't even imagine,

00:08:12.764 --> 00:08:14.901
'cause everyone will
maximize their productivity.

00:08:14.901 --> 00:08:17.486
- Large uninterrupted blocks of time,

00:08:17.486 --> 00:08:19.828
you have to schedule,
if you are a creator.

00:08:19.828 --> 00:08:22.714
Blocks of time that are at
least two to four hours,

00:08:22.714 --> 00:08:23.921
or more, in length.

00:08:23.921 --> 00:08:27.449
No Frankenstein monster
of 20-minute breaks

00:08:27.449 --> 00:08:30.170
and 10-minute breaks,
combined into three hours,

00:08:30.170 --> 00:08:32.892
will have the value of
an uninterrupted block

00:08:32.892 --> 00:08:34.050
of three hours

00:08:34.050 --> 00:08:36.849
if you are trying to make
high-level decisions,

00:08:36.849 --> 00:08:40.677
focus on time-consuming,
high-priority projects,

00:08:40.677 --> 00:08:43.301
push something to a next milestone,

00:08:43.301 --> 00:08:45.008
as a maker, creator.

00:08:45.008 --> 00:08:46.986
We all have the same 24 hours in the day,

00:08:46.986 --> 00:08:49.000
and if you're like, I don't have time,

00:08:49.000 --> 00:08:50.702
I can't sleep, I need
to cut back on sleep,

00:08:50.702 --> 00:08:52.352
I need to do this, I need to do that,

00:08:52.352 --> 00:08:55.550
if you don't have time,
you don't have priorities.

00:08:55.550 --> 00:08:56.383
That's it.

00:08:56.383 --> 00:08:58.877
- Writing in a journal allows you

00:08:58.877 --> 00:09:01.422
to record your daily progress.

00:09:01.422 --> 00:09:03.050
There's a lot of scientific research

00:09:03.050 --> 00:09:04.888
on the small win theory.

00:09:04.888 --> 00:09:07.696
And what it says is this:
if every single day,

00:09:07.696 --> 00:09:10.443
you record small daily acts of progress,

00:09:10.443 --> 00:09:12.596
you actually dump dopamine,

00:09:12.596 --> 00:09:15.080
a neurotransmitter, into your brain,

00:09:15.080 --> 00:09:17.169
and that is a great source of motivation.

00:09:17.169 --> 00:09:19.312
You feel happy and you feel strong,

00:09:19.312 --> 00:09:20.546
and you feel inspired.

00:09:20.546 --> 00:09:23.065
So every single morning,
in your holy hour,

00:09:23.065 --> 00:09:25.698
from five to six, take 20 minutes,

00:09:25.698 --> 00:09:29.944
record your wins of the
previous day, in your journal.

00:09:29.944 --> 00:09:32.977
It'll keep you motivated,
it'll make you feel

00:09:32.977 --> 00:09:34.882
like you're making progress,

00:09:34.882 --> 00:09:36.495
it'll keep you inspired,

00:09:36.495 --> 00:09:39.318
versus always feeling like
you're never achieving enough.

00:09:39.318 --> 00:09:41.168
- What do you suggest, Mel,

00:09:41.168 --> 00:09:43.485
for accessing what you really want?

00:09:43.485 --> 00:09:45.627
You know, I talk a lot about
being honest with yourself

00:09:45.627 --> 00:09:47.366
about what you want,
and if you're somebody

00:09:47.366 --> 00:09:50.450
that's watching this and you
have no clue what you want,

00:09:50.450 --> 00:09:52.228
I'm going to say that's total bull.

00:09:52.228 --> 00:09:54.582
I think you've probably
decided that either

00:09:54.582 --> 00:09:56.635
you can't have it, because you don't think

00:09:56.635 --> 00:09:59.600
you're smart enough or good
enough, or worthy enough,

00:09:59.600 --> 00:10:01.324
or maybe you think you're too old,

00:10:01.324 --> 00:10:02.596
or you've told yourself

00:10:02.596 --> 00:10:04.764
that you can't make a living doing it.

00:10:04.764 --> 00:10:07.421
Both are complete and utter lies

00:10:07.421 --> 00:10:09.236
that you're telling yourself.

00:10:09.236 --> 00:10:11.226
What you need to do is ask yourself this:

00:10:11.226 --> 00:10:12.773
if you took money off the table,

00:10:12.773 --> 00:10:15.396
if you didn't give a what
anybody else thought,

00:10:15.396 --> 00:10:18.019
what's the thing you would love
to be doing with your life?

00:10:18.019 --> 00:10:18.998
Seriously.

00:10:18.998 --> 00:10:21.240
Do you dream of being a
professional photographer?

00:10:21.240 --> 00:10:22.965
Do you want to open your own restaurant?

00:10:22.965 --> 00:10:25.032
Have you always thought
about traveling the world

00:10:25.032 --> 00:10:28.397
and entertaining kids
with your juggling skills?

00:10:28.397 --> 00:10:30.388
I don't know, it's your life.

00:10:30.388 --> 00:10:33.008
You get to choose what you want to do.

00:10:33.008 --> 00:10:34.808
Be honest with yourself.

00:10:34.808 --> 00:10:38.183
What is it that you would
want to do with your life,

00:10:38.183 --> 00:10:40.954
if you didn't have to
pay the bills doing it?

00:10:40.954 --> 00:10:42.339
Another thing you can ask yourself:

00:10:42.339 --> 00:10:44.483
who do you find yourself
sort of envious of?

00:10:44.483 --> 00:10:45.919
You know, like you look at their life,

00:10:45.919 --> 00:10:48.075
and you just think, gosh, how awesome

00:10:48.075 --> 00:10:49.990
that they get to do that.

00:10:49.990 --> 00:10:52.837
Well once you have that
answer for yourself,

00:10:52.837 --> 00:10:54.574
you've gotten really
honest, you've pushed the

00:10:54.574 --> 00:10:57.876
aside, and you've really
asked it for yourself

00:10:57.876 --> 00:11:00.039
and answered the question honestly,

00:11:00.039 --> 00:11:02.003
all you got to do is
explore it, that's it.

00:11:02.003 --> 00:11:06.278
Just find one thing that
you can do to enrich

00:11:06.278 --> 00:11:09.025
and expand your knowledge
about it, find one course

00:11:09.025 --> 00:11:11.707
online, Google the topic, stalk people

00:11:11.707 --> 00:11:14.076
that are pursuing this line of work.

00:11:14.076 --> 00:11:17.578
That's how you start to do it.

00:11:17.578 --> 00:11:19.016
One step at a time.

00:11:19.016 --> 00:11:20.866
So start with answering the question,

00:11:20.866 --> 00:11:23.713
what do you really want, with
a massive dose of honesty,

00:11:23.713 --> 00:11:26.674
Google the topic, and find one thing

00:11:26.674 --> 00:11:28.220
that you can do, just one.

00:11:28.220 --> 00:11:30.933
Push yourself, and start to explore.

00:11:30.933 --> 00:11:33.728
If you were to wake up and
do that every single day,

00:11:33.728 --> 00:11:37.706
spend 10 minutes a day,
you would be startled,

00:11:37.706 --> 00:11:39.735
astonished by what your life looks like

00:11:39.735 --> 00:11:41.740
in a matter of a year or two.

00:11:41.740 --> 00:11:43.970
- Never lose hope.

00:11:43.970 --> 00:11:46.859
That you have a single breath
within your body right now,

00:11:46.859 --> 00:11:49.982
and that you are alive
in this moment, is hope.

00:11:49.982 --> 00:11:52.375
That you can see all these
people walking on the street,

00:11:52.375 --> 00:11:54.662
smiling, is hope.

00:11:54.662 --> 00:11:56.654
That all these entrepreneurs
are posting their art

00:11:56.654 --> 00:12:00.169
online, every single day
now, there is hope there.

00:12:00.169 --> 00:12:02.689
That there is a single
person out in this world

00:12:02.689 --> 00:12:05.131
whose soul is still burning alive

00:12:05.131 --> 00:12:07.828
with love, is hope.

00:12:07.828 --> 00:12:10.199
You know, it's so easy during these days,

00:12:10.199 --> 00:12:12.339
when sometimes there's
darkness, when you see

00:12:12.339 --> 00:12:13.626
all this negative media coverage,

00:12:13.626 --> 00:12:15.402
or maybe you have a series of bad days,

00:12:15.402 --> 00:12:17.345
or a series of bad weeks,

00:12:17.345 --> 00:12:19.736
or your lucky break just isn't coming,

00:12:19.736 --> 00:12:21.442
or you've been fighting for that dream,

00:12:21.442 --> 00:12:23.443
you just don't sense any of that progress

00:12:23.443 --> 00:12:26.809
that you just so need
to feel still enlivened,

00:12:26.809 --> 00:12:29.113
and engaged, and
enthusiastic about something,

00:12:29.113 --> 00:12:31.919
or somebody breaks up with
you, or you lose your job,

00:12:31.919 --> 00:12:34.062
or something happens with your health.

00:12:34.062 --> 00:12:35.991
Look, that's part of life,

00:12:35.991 --> 00:12:39.406
is there's going to be so many
struggles and disappointments,

00:12:39.406 --> 00:12:42.819
challenges, set-backs, dark days.

00:12:42.819 --> 00:12:46.007
And part of sustaining, and
making through all of that

00:12:46.007 --> 00:12:48.850
is maintaining hope,

00:12:48.850 --> 00:12:50.943
and that hope isn't something
that just, you know,

00:12:50.943 --> 00:12:52.881
some airy-fairy concept.

00:12:52.881 --> 00:12:55.073
It is a psychological need

00:12:55.073 --> 00:12:57.430
to believe that we can endure,

00:12:57.430 --> 00:12:58.777
a psychological need to believe

00:12:58.777 --> 00:13:00.766
that we can not only
endure, but we can succeed

00:13:00.766 --> 00:13:04.372
and we can thrive, and we
can have our way in the world

00:13:04.372 --> 00:13:05.984
so that we can accomplish our dream,

00:13:05.984 --> 00:13:07.367
so that we can make influence,

00:13:07.367 --> 00:13:09.258
make our own difference.

00:13:09.258 --> 00:13:12.229
So, have hope, but even as I say that,

00:13:12.229 --> 00:13:14.739
let me reconfigure that
statement and that phrase,

00:13:14.739 --> 00:13:17.598
because too many people
say well you have hope

00:13:17.598 --> 00:13:19.325
or you can lose hope,

00:13:19.325 --> 00:13:21.214
but hope isn't something actually

00:13:21.214 --> 00:13:25.268
you have or that you lose,
even though we say that phrase

00:13:25.268 --> 00:13:27.032
at such a popular level.

00:13:27.032 --> 00:13:30.535
You know, years ago, a
metaphor came into my life,

00:13:30.535 --> 00:13:32.237
that changed my life forever.

00:13:32.237 --> 00:13:35.634
It changed my attitude and my actions,

00:13:35.634 --> 00:13:37.222
and how I thought about life,

00:13:37.222 --> 00:13:41.368
and frankly, how I felt every
single moment of the day.

00:13:41.368 --> 00:13:43.974
It was something that lifted
me to a whole 'nother level

00:13:43.974 --> 00:13:46.676
of joy and vibrancy in life,

00:13:46.676 --> 00:13:48.380
and it was this very simple metaphor

00:13:48.380 --> 00:13:52.349
that the power plant doesn't have energy,

00:13:52.349 --> 00:13:56.572
it transforms and generates energy.

00:13:56.572 --> 00:13:57.822
Let me say that again.

00:13:57.822 --> 00:14:00.228
The power plant doesn't have energy,

00:14:00.228 --> 00:14:03.802
it transforms and generates energy.

00:14:03.802 --> 00:14:07.771
At the same level, we don't
quote-unquote have hope,

00:14:07.771 --> 00:14:09.915
we transform the energy around us,

00:14:09.915 --> 00:14:11.626
we generate hope.

00:14:11.626 --> 00:14:15.041
We don't have happiness,
we generate happiness.

00:14:15.041 --> 00:14:18.316
Similarly, we don't
have sadness or fatigue,

00:14:18.316 --> 00:14:20.986
we don't have those feelings
that so many people think

00:14:20.986 --> 00:14:23.088
are negative, that just land on them.

00:14:23.088 --> 00:14:26.428
We are in our own
actions, our own thoughts,

00:14:26.428 --> 00:14:28.167
our own interpretations,

00:14:28.167 --> 00:14:31.530
the very thoughts that we
are feeding our psyche.

00:14:31.530 --> 00:14:34.630
Those very things, those
are generating an emotion,

00:14:34.630 --> 00:14:37.970
and hope is something
that is generated by us.

00:14:37.970 --> 00:14:39.859
When it feels like it is gone,

00:14:39.859 --> 00:14:43.661
that becomes a to-do list for
us to generate it once more,

00:14:43.661 --> 00:14:45.386
just like when your phone is dying,

00:14:45.386 --> 00:14:47.265
you plug it in to charge it up.

00:14:47.265 --> 00:14:49.557
Well, when your hope is dying,

00:14:49.557 --> 00:14:52.518
it's time to generate it
and charge it up again.

00:14:52.518 --> 00:14:54.924
Same thing with happiness, and aliveness,

00:14:54.924 --> 00:14:56.686
and enthusiasm, those are things,

00:14:56.686 --> 00:14:59.094
when they're going down,
you got to get focused,

00:14:59.094 --> 00:15:01.248
you got to plug back in to your passions,

00:15:01.248 --> 00:15:03.629
to your dreams, to tomorrow,

00:15:03.629 --> 00:15:06.379
to charge yourself back up again.

00:15:07.850 --> 00:15:09.333
